SM(390,{"n":"Deuteronomy 4 Part 2","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Deuteronomy 4 Part 2.mp3","d":2858.1,"s":[[0.32,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[9.04,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in biblical studies, and it's an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[22.64,"Verse 14. Then the Lord commanded me at that time to teach you ordinances and judgments, so you might observe them in the land you are crossing over to inherit."],[32.16,"So be careful to guard your souls, for you saw no form when the Lord spoke to you at Horeb on the mountain from the midst of the fire."],[40.4,"Do not act lawlessly, and make for yourselves a carved form of any image, the likeness of male or female, the likeness of any cattle on the earth, or the likeness of any winged bird that flies under heaven, the likeness of anything that creeps on the ground, or the likeness of any fish in the waters beneath the earth."],[60.68,"Okay. So, what does he say to them?"],[63.32,"He says, When you were there, remember, you didn't see anybody."],[66.44,"Now, this is interest."],[69.18,"Let's push on this a little."],[71.26,"He says, You didn't see anybody, and that's true."],[73.42,"Did Moses see somebody?"],[75.58,"Yes. Moses saw somebody."],[77.98,"But Moses didn't make any images."],[80.64,"Of that person."],[81.76,"Um, otherwise we'd have way older icons of Christ than we actually do."],[85.84,"But uh Moses, but he's saying, you you folks didn't."],[90.25,"You folks didn't."],[92.17,"Therefore. Therefore, and there is this relative statement here that this is the reason why they are not to make any images of what?"],[102.75,"Of God Because there is that relative statement of therefore."],[110.21,"It would not make sense to say when we were at Mount Horeb and you saw the fire and heard the thunder and the voice, you did not see the form of God, therefore you are not allowed to draw a picture of your pet goldfish."],[123.99,"That doesn't make any logical sense."],[126.17,"So this isn't saying you can't draw a picture of anything."],[129.94,"This isn't saying you can't, draw a picture of your dad."],[134.38,"This is talking about depicting God."],[138.22,"And the things they list."],[141.42,"Let's talk about idolatry."],[143.5,"These are forms that the nations surrounding them gave to the divine, gave to gods, the gods that they worshiped."],[152.6,"So he is precluding like what they did with the golden calf, remember?"],[156.76,"Aaron didn't make a bowl and be like, hey, let's all worship Baal now."],[162.36,"He made a golden calf, he made a bowl, and he said, This is Yahweh who brought you out of Egypt."],[170.9,"So this is talking about not making depictions of God because they had not seen him."],[178.66,"And this is part of that principle of imagination."],[183.43,"That's that's at the core of this."],[186.31,"The core of this is the idea that of humans trying to make God in their image by their own imagination."],[201.15,"But is appealing to humans because the whole purpose of idolatry was that the idols were used to manipulate and control the gods."],[210.11,"Now they did that in a very literal ritual sense."],[212.61,"We bring you these offerings, you give us this in return with the pagan gods."],[217.03,"But it also happened in a more subtle sense."],[220.25,"In the more subtle sense that I come up with my idea of who God is, and I come up with an idea of God that is very congenial to me."],[230.41,"So this is this is is something that still very pertinent to us today."],[234.23,"Lots of people have their own personal Jesus."],[237.52,"Someone to hear their prayers, someone who cares."],[239.44,"Anyway, uh, who they've invented in their invented in their mind."],[245.94,"Who just loves them just the way they are."],[248.98,"And never asks them to do anything they don't want to do."],[253.0,"And is always on their side."],[255.0,"And surely, no matter what they do and how they live, is gonna take them to heaven when they die."],[259.88,"And loves everything they love, pistachio ice cream, and hates everything they hate, like broccoli."],[267.53,"Just that's their image."],[269.93,"And they do it in unsubtle ways."],[273.3,"Uh there were three quests for the historical Jesus, where very smart scholars did this."],[284.26,"Created these versions of Jesus that they said were the real Jesus, who all looked a lot like them."],[292.67,"If they were kind of charismatic, then Jesus was seemed kind of charismatic, you know."],[297.55,"And if they were, you know, a little more Roman Catholic and ascetical, then Jesus seemed real kind of more ascetical and strict, you know, and just sort of however they kind of wanted him to be."],[310.25,"And so this is something humans are prone to."],[312.67,"And so God is ruling this out."],[316.13,"And Moses is advising them to rule this out."],[319.21,"Because that God, number one, or that Jesus, doesn't exist, therefore can't save you, can't help you."],[327.77,"You can't follow him because he's not leading you anywhere, because you've made him exactly where you are right now."],[334.57,"So you can't follow him anywhere in terms of growing, changing, repenting, or anything."],[340.54,"And so having that as your God is gonna lead you in the exact other direction."],[349.26,"It's gonna lead you deeper into your sin."],[351.42,"It's gonna lead you on the path to condemnation, on the path to destruction."],[359.34,"So Moses is saying, don't go there."],[360.54,"'t Don go there."],[362.74,"Okay? And this passage gets brought up in the eighth century when there starts to be arguments about iconography."],[373.87,"And the church fathers are very quick to point out this is why icons of Christ in particular are so closely related to our understanding of Christ's incarnation."],[386.37,"Is they will point to this verse and say, Yes, at that time they saw no form."],[390.93,"We saw Jesus."],[393.73,"And that's not just a rhetorical point."],[396.93,"That's over and over again in the New Testament."],[399.97,"The end of St."],[400.77,"John's prologue at the beginning of his gospel."],[403.09,"No one has seen God at any time."],[406.09,"But the unique Son who is in the bosom of the Father has made him known."],[410.33,"St. Peter, what we have seen, what we have touched with our hands, what we made known to you."],[415.91,"Like this is a theological point made by the New Testament that this has changed."],[421.83,"That now the people of God have all seen God."],[425.88,"And this is why our rules about iconography are that you can only depict Christ as Christ, as he appeared in to, Orthodox iconography, depict him as a sheep."],[444.64,"It's very common in the West."],[446.24,"I know. It seems crazy, but. you're not allowed to depict him as a sheep"],[451.76,"Okay? Orthodox iconography actually kind of takes this to the point of kind of weirdness."],[457.84,"Okay. There is a major icon, that depicts a patent."],[464.94,"The discos. That we have the lamb on in the Eucharist."],[470.74,"And in the icon, it does not show the piece of bread."],[477.46,"It shows a tiny Jesus."],[481.54,"A tiny depiction of Christ on the discos."],[484.34,"Why? Because it's an icon, and you're only allowed to depict Christ as Christ."],[490.84,"And so after its consecration, that lamb is Christ, so he has to be depicted in a icon as Christ."],[497.36,"That's how strict this rule is."],[501.5,"And so, and in terms of iconography of the saints and other figures of the Bible, this text says nothing about that."],[509.11,"That's not idolatry."],[512.39,"I had someone who was gonna try and make a case from the church fathers to me against iconography."],[519.43,"And all the quotes he were given, he was giving me were church fathers criticizing pagans for depicting the divine in the form of humans and animals."],[532.87,"Like this. Exactly what Moses critiqued."],[534.81,"I'm like, and I kind of St"],[535.09,"And I said, that's not what iconography is."],[540.45,"Paul is like a portrait of St."],[543.57,"Paul, who was a human that he's portrayed as a human who looks like St."],[549.01,"Paul did. That's not, and even even Christ, Christ is divine, but we're not just like making up imagining what he looked like or depicting him as an animal, or right, it's Christ as he as he appeared."],[568.8,"So this the in one sense."],[573.81,"What happens in Christ kind of changes this in the sense that now we have a way of depicting God, namely our Lord Jesus Christ."],[581.86,"But in another sense, this hasn't changed at all."],[584.6,"This is still the principle."],[587.66,"The exclusion of imagination, the exclusion of idolatry."],[590.8,"That's all still fully accepted by us."],[594.58,"The principles here."],[595.54,"Yes, sir. So how did I just I'm curious, um, how did Roman depictions of Jesus, Roman Catholic depictions of Jesus, come stray from the truth?"],[607.94,"Yeah. So the Pope accepted and then rejected and then accepted again, the Seventh Ecumenical Council."],[615.62,"That was the council in 787 that dealt with iconography."],[620.74,"And the reason it got accepted and then not accepted and then accepted again was Charlemagne."],[629.34,"Who didn't like it."],[630.7,"He didn't like icons?"],[632.78,"No, he didn't like the theology, the positive theology of icons."],[638.46,"That was given there."],[639.58,"So part of the debate was about whether the Eucharist was an icon."],[644.22,"So the iconoclast said the only real icon of Christ is the Eucharist, because an icon has to be homoousios with its prototype."],[656.14,"That's something they made up, but"],[658.3,"And so one of the things that uh the Seondc council of Nicaea affirmed was that the Eucharist is not an icon."],[665.26,"It's not something you look at"],[665.54,"The Eucharist is another thing."],[669.2,"Well, the the West already disagreed on that."],[673.92,"So that was one of the major points of disagreement."],[676.16,"They want to say the Eucharist was an icon."],[680.24,"And they also didn't take the accept the positive view of iconography that was put forth by the 7th and 8th ecumenical councils."],[693.28,"Yes, there was an eighth one in the ninth century that also dealt with this."],[698.32,"But because in the sense that for them, iconography was primarily just art that was used for educational purposes."],[712.38,"And so they didn't have the problem with imagination that the East did."],[718.7,"Which I would argue is coming from here in Deuteronomy."],[723.5,"And so what ends up happening in the Libri Carolini, in a in a series of councils, Western Frankish councils, uh Charlemagne's court theologians put forward a different theology of iconography."],[736.54,"And that goes in two directions."],[737.98,"Number one, that's where Eucharistic adoration starts in the Roman Catholic Church, where you have the Eucharist being elevated and put into monstrance and people worshiping it, which was never a thing in the East."],[751.84,"Because we're like the Eucharist is for eating, not looking at."],[756.28,"And then that also, then so the Eucharist goes, Eucharistic adoration goes in that direction, and then in the other direction, art, just becomes sort of art, and imagination is allowed."],[770.38,"And so if you look at the very early Western art, it looks very similar to a lot of iconography, at least in the broad strokes."],[786.38,"Well, no, but you see all the you you see images of you know the Theotokos and Christ as an infant."],[792.07,"In roughly the same pose as in an icon."],[794.69,"But you start to see elements of imagination coming in different colors. more realistic faces"],[801.13,"Um by the time you get to the Renaissance, they're using like live people as models for how they depict saints and stuff."],[810.01,"Yeah, perspective, um, lots of other imaginative elements."],[814.41,"And so, but that's because there's this more loose view, of iconography."],[820.51,"Whereas in the East, there's a very tight so in the East, you can have Christian art."],[824.67,"That's fine, but it's not an i it's not iconography."],[828.17,"Iconography has to follow very strict rules of color, of presentation, of everything."],[834.57,"And so you could have heretical iconography."],[838.93,"That's communicating bad theology, theoretically, from our perspective."],[843.17,"There's also like a weird, like you're talking about the realism."],[845.57,"There's like a weird kind of mass."],[847.25,"I think some of that's just like the West in general at that time."],[850.13,"There's like a weird discussion with realism."],[851.97,"So they even forget what a halo is."],[854.77,"Like so you look at the halos and R."],[856.53,"Yeah. The nimbus, yeah."],[858.37,"Moses is more."],[863.81,"The glory of God reflected in their face."],[865.97,"And so then you start seeing it be like the little circle floating circle."],[870.21,"Because they don't know how they forgot what it's about, and so they think it's gotta be this like little thing."],[875.09,"And so then you get to like later where it's just like you know, just a little the cartoon version of like a little golden ring above your head."],[883.17,"Yeah, Michelangelo's Moses with horns because of a mistranslation of of uh part the Torah."],[892.09,"So, yeah, so you get that."],[893.85,"So they have a much looser view of iconography."],[898.73,"Um iconography was never never had the pronounced role in the West that it had in the east."],[905.85,"In the West, in the East we have relics, but the veneration of relics was much bigger in the West than the East."],[915.93,"And the veneration of iconography, I'm talking about pre-1000, and the veneration of uh icons was bigger in the east than of the West, than in the West pre 1000."],[927.29,"And so because of that, the West had a much looser view of an iconography, and that sort of got ratified by the Eighth Ecumen or Eighth Ecumenical Council, or Seventh Ecumenical Council getting accepted kind of through a lens, of interpretation in the West."],[950.39,"So yeah, that's sort of how that happened."],[952.47,"And that's sort of how they end up with statues, and we don't."],[955.59,"There is no rule in the Orthodox Church that you can't have a statue, hypothetically."],[961.11,"But there is a rule that our iconography has to follow the ancient models."],[967.03,"Can't use imagination, you have to follow ancient models, and we don't have any ancient models of statuary to follow."],[973.75,"So sort of de facto, if an Orthodox artist wanted to make a statue, it couldn't qualify as an icon because you couldn't demonstrate that it was following the ancient models."],[985.71,"You would have to do it imaginatively."],[988.67,"But if we had, if we dug up tomorrow, you know, a uh second century statue right of a saint or something, people could reproduce it."],[1002.34,"And you could make an argument that it could be valid as that ICA because it's following an ancient model."],[1006.74,"We have bas relief, we have things that are somewhat three-dimensional."],[1010.0,"Because we just we don't have the ancient examples."],[1014.24,"Yes, sir? You had a question."],[1016.8,"Oh, um. do Do they they st stillill in the Roman church, believe that the Eucharist is an icon?"],[1025.8,"And if so, is it an icon and something else?"],[1029.16,"Or how could it be icon and still have the real presence?"],[1032.52,"Well, in Eucharistic adoration, it's treated as one."],[1039.34,"In the sense that it's right, people except that they they worship it rather than venerating it because they say it's Christ himself."],[1050.11,"And there's a lot of other Eucharistic theology developments there too."],[1053.84,"This is all very shorthand."],[1055.38,"Because now they will say that just the host is the body, blood, soul, and divinity of Christ."],[1061.98,"Which is like gobbledygook to us."],[1063.86,"Like, he said, This is my body, not this is my body, blood, soul, and divinity"],[1070.06,"Well, yeah, because they may they make these sort of logical arguments like, well, you can't separate Christ's body and blood."],[1075.82,"Like, as if that's what we're doing."],[1078.32,"Like, or you can't separate his body and blood from his divinity."],[1082.16,"It's like we're not Nestorians, we're not separating them."],[1085.68,"We're just he said, This is my body."],[1087.84,"So we're saying, yes, it really is his body."],[1092.24,"Okay, verse 19."],[1093.76,"So idolatry, right out."],[1098.48,"Also, do not act lawlessly when you lift your eyes to heaven and see the sun, the moon, and the stars."],[1105.76,"All the adornment of heaven, and you thus go astray and worship and serve them, which the Lord your God assigned to all the nations under heaven."],[1118.52,"Okay, let's pause there."],[1121.24,"I'm curious. Now I have to look at the uh I know I'm not gonna like what I find here, but oh yeah, that footnote's horrible."],[1133.0,"Okay. Uh that's so uh so part of the problem with with our understanding what Moses is saying here is that we look at the sun, moon, and stars very differently than ancient people did."],[1148.3,"So we know that the the moon is a kind of a big rock that orbits around the Earth."],[1152.38,"Let me offend some more people"],[1156.34,"There's now offended flat earthers."],[1159.46,"We've landed on it."],[1163.38,"We've landed on it."],[1165.3,"The Chinese have rovers on it right now today, rolling around, sending back video."],[1170.02,"It's not made too much."],[1175.44,"But we kind of know that's what it is."],[1177.81,"And you know, the sun is either a massive incandescent gas or a miasma of incandescent plasma, depending on which they might be giants release you're listening to."],[1187.75,"We know they're they're, you know, stars are made of plasma, that there are uh hyd.rogen fusion reactions into helium going on at the core of them"],[1200.59,"They put out light D."],[1202.32,"We know these things."],[1203.84,"That's not at all how ancient people looked at them, and that's not at all what Moses is talking about."],[1207.92,"That there are people modern readers of this want to lump this together with the old thing."],[1211.36,"They're like, yeah, don't make idols and worship rocks and sticks."],[1214.4,"And guess what?"],[1215.2,"Those are like rocks and sticks in space."],[1217.04,"Don't worship those either."],[1219.02,"But that's not that's not that's not uh how anybody who wrote this or originally heard this or read this thought."],[1229.98,"These are, to put a fine point on it, these are angels."],[1235.04,"As far as any ancient person or gods, if you're a pagan, ancient pagan."],[1239.44,"Um moving around, in the heavens"],[1245.14,"There are spirits associated with these things."],[1249.08,"So I think we talked about this a little back in Genesis 1, when it talked about on the fourth day, God create when God created the sun, moon, and the stars, that he created them to govern the day and the night, respectively."],[1262.92,"That that was not just like, oh, it looks like the sun's in charge up there during the day."],[1267.54,"Uh that the moon's real big at night."],[1270.58,"That this was talking about, and this is the way the fathers, this is one of the days where the fathers say the angels were created."],[1276.98,"The church fathers usually say either the first day or the fourth day, which are connected."],[1281.74,"One is where light is created, and one is where the lights in particular are created."],[1285.9,"That's when the angels are created."],[1320.3,"Other parts of his administration."],[1322.5,"And you say, why does God need that?"],[1327.38,"And I say to you, he doesn't."],[1331.54,"God doesn't need that."],[1334.18,"But, but just like God doesn't need me or you."],[1338.5,"God doesn't need anything or anyone."],[1341.52,"Still created us."],[1343.68,"Why? Out of love."],[1347.21,"Out of love."],[1348.49,"God can heal a person without me praying for them."],[1354.09,"It's not like if I don't pray, if we don't get enough likes on this Facebook post, the kid's gonna die of cancer."],[1359.31,"That's not how it works."],[1361.36,"Like, he doesn't need me to pray for somebody."],[1364.0,"He can just heal them."],[1366.4,"But he gives me the privilege."],[1368.82,"Sometimes of, working through my and other people's prayers to heal someone."],[1369.98,"So I get to be a part of God's healing"],[1375.46,"I get to be a part of the good things God does on earth."],[1378.26,"He created the angels for the same reason."],[1381.06,"He doesn't need angels."],[1383.86,"Okay. We've been reading that God shows up all the time in person and talks to people, including Moses."],[1398.04,"So it's got nothing to do with that."],[1399.72,"There is no need, there is no necessity."],[1401.72,"But God, out of love, creates beings other than himself."],[1406.28,"And out of his love for them, he shares with them."],[1409.25,"Allows them to participate in his life, to share his life."],[1413.69,"And so that takes the form of this kind of governance and administration."],[1417.77,"And this is the promise to humans."],[1421.63,"This is where our whole concept of salvation is theosis comes from."],[1426.43,"That humans, when they're glorified after their death, God gives them a place in his."],[1432.49,"This is remember back in Revelation."],[1435.85,"Say to die during this time, come alive and rule and reign with Christ."],[1442.43,"Christ doesn't need co rulers."],[1444.35,"He can rule the world all by himself."],[1446.11,"Christ can be king all by himself if he wants to."],[1448.83,"But out of love, he shares that."],[1451.95,"He shares that."],[1453.63,"And so what Philo says is being pointed out here is that God assigned these angelic beings."],[1458.11,"We're going to read more about this when we get to the end of Deuteronomy, and we'll talk more about it there"],[1465.67,"But God assigned these angelic beings to help him govern the whole world, all the nations."],[1471.45,"And what Philo is going to point out is that the other nations start to worship these beings as gods in their majesty and give glory to the God who created them."],[1496.17,"But start worshipping them in their own right."],[1498.57,"Start thinking that they, in their own right, control the destiny of humans on earth."],[1501.05,"Think astrology Which was way bigger in the ancient world than it is now."],[1512.19,"They control things."],[1514.43,"That you need to worship them."],[1516.19,"That you need to."],[1517.6,"Which is a basic mistake."],[1519.52,"They give God's glory to someone else, to a created being."],[1526.24,"So Moses is saying they do that."],[1531.44,"You don't do that."],[1534.64,"And so it's not just a question of don't worship the sun."],[1539.74,"Don't worship sun gods, don't worship moon gods."],[1542.62,"But it's all of them."],[1544.14,"What all of the pagans have in common is that they're worshiping these other spirits."],[1550.9,"Who are spirits who God created."],[1554.42,"They're creatures just like you and me."],[1557.16,"And when a good angel shows up."],[1559.17,"When an angel who comes from God shows up in the Bible, what's the first thing he says?"],[1563.97,"Because somebody falls down and tries to worship him almost immediately."],[1567.17,"And what does he say?"],[1568.13,"He says, get up off the ground."],[1569.41,"Don't I'm a created being just like you."],[1574.05,"Don't, you know, I'm a servant of God just like you."],[1576.21,"Don't worship me."],[1577.57,"Worship him. So that's what that's what he's talking about here."],[1584.74,"So, and this is true all through the scriptures."],[1587.62,"It's gonna be true all through the Bible"],[1588.32,"We saw it in Revelation not that long ago because we looped around, but it's true here in the Torah."],[1594.64,"When it's talking about stars, it's almost always talking about angels."],[1600.32,"Almost always. Talking talking about angels."],[1603.97,"And that's how ancient people uh would have understood it."],[1608.85,"So it's don't try to worship God using idols."],[1615.73,"Was that first piece?"],[1616.85,"And now it's don't worship other gods."],[1619.57,"Don't worship the other gods that the nations worship."],[1623.97,"And the reason why is not, again, as we've already seen through the whole Torah, not because they're imaginary, not because they don't exist."],[1631.27,"But because they're spirits who are created by God, just like you, you worship the true God, you don't worship them."],[1638.07,"Verse 20. But so now this is the difference."],[1640.47,"He's saying they're worshipped by the other nations."],[1642.95,"But but the Lord took you and brought you out of the iron furnace from Egypt to be his people, an inheritance, as you are this day."],[1653.35,"Furthermore, the Lord was angry with me about what you said, and swore I would not cross over the Jordan and enter the land of the Lord your God is giving you as an inheritance."],[1663.19,"But I am going to die in this land, but I am not going to cross over this Jordan, but you will cross over and inherit this good land."],[1672.15,"Take heed to yourselves, lest you forget the covenant the Lord your God made with you, and make for yourselves a carved form of anything concerning which the Lord your God forbade you."],[1682.75,"For the Lord your God is a consuming fire, a jealous God."],[1686.03,"So he's saying, Look, yes, the other nations do that, but you're not like the other nations."],[1693.79,"God didn't go and rescue the other nations out of Egypt, out of slavery."],[1698.43,"God didn't form them out of nothing."],[1701.67,"In the same way he formed Israel as a nation out of nothing."],[1705.19,"Not them as individual people, but the nation."],[1708.21,"Remember, God didn't choose one of the nations to be his."],[1711.33,"He made a new one."],[1712.87,"Through this whole process since Exodus that we've been reading."],[1715.77,"And so you don't do what they do."],[1718.11,"You're different. God has revealed himself to you directly, so you worship just him."],[1723.44,"Because he will not tolerate you trying to bring in and also worship these other spirits who he created."],[1730.4,"Verse 25 If you beget sons and the sons of sons, and dwell a long time in the land, and act lawlessly, and make a carved form of anything, and do evil in the sight of the Lord your God to provoke him to anger."],[1743.44,"I call heaven and earth to witness to you today that you will be utterly destroyed from the land you are crossing over the Jordan to inherit."],[1750.88,"You will not live long on it, but will be utterly annihilated."],[1754.32,"So Moses here is being really mean."],[1756.32,"We can't have this."],[1757.92,"We all need to be nice."],[1760.08,"Uh but uh Moses isn't like cursing them."],[1766.54,"But he is saying a curse is gonna come upon them if they if they do this."],[1771.15,"And he's got he calls two witnesses."],[1773.71,"Remember, this is how we establish anything in court in the Torah."],[1777.71,"You have to have two witnesses who give the same testimony."],[1781.17,"He says, The heavens up above, the earth you're living on."],[1786.37,"They're gonna know what you do when you get into the land."],[1791.33,"And if you disobey all this, you're gonna get wiped out."],[1797.25,"Why is why is this so important?"],[1799.01,"And why is he using such drastic?"],[1801.73,"Well, because what are they about to do?"],[1805.57,"They're about to go into the land, and some of the people, not all of them, but certain groups, they're gonna wipe out."],[1813.87,"They're gonna wipe out."],[1815.07,"And God is saying, if you become like them, you're gonna get wiped out too."],[1823.31,"So a lot of what we've been reading, here in these these first four chapters of Deuteronomy."],[1830.7,"We've talked about this especially in terms of chapter two."],[1833.98,"Is again, Moses keeps is telling Israel over and over again in different ways, you're special, but you're not special."],[1843.15,"You're special in certain ways."],[1846.72,"But that doesn't mean."],[1848.7,"So the fact that God loved you and made you into this special people and did these things or bring you out of Egypt and all this doesn't mean if you're wicked, if you're evil, if you're disobedient, he's gonna let it slide more than he lets these other nations slide."],[1863.99,"In fact, quite the opposite."],[1866.79,"The fact that you're the only nation on earth that is to receive the Torah, that you're the only nation on earth that has God dwelling in your midst, that you're only the only nation of the world to which God is sending prophets."],[1877.19,"That makes you more accountable and more responsible than those other nations."],[1882.47,"So you should expect less patience."],[1886.01,"You should expect more accountability."],[1889.05,"And this is the same argument St."],[1890.81,"Paul is making in Romans 1 and 2."],[1892.41,"He's saying, yes, the Jewish people are special"],[1894.07,"He's getting this from Deuteronomy."],[1898.95,"They received the Torah, they received the prophets, they received right, all these things."],[1903.49,"But if you don't keep it, St."],[1905.97,"Paul says, it's not the hearers of the law, it's the doers of the law."],[1911.01,"The fact that you went to the synagogue and heard the commandments every Sabbath doesn't mean anything if you didn't do anything, do it."],[1921.17,"You're not better off than some Roman who didn't do it."],[1924.85,"You're in the same boat as the Roman who didn't do it."],[1927.09,"In fact, the Roman might be due more mercy because he at least never heard it."],[1931.97,"He at least kind of has an excuse."],[1936.22,"And you don't."],[1938.86,"So that's a lot of the theme here."],[1942.66,"And this is going to continue in Deuteronomy."],[1945.54,"This is going to be an ongoing theme woven through."],[1949.46,"You're special. You have a special destiny."],[1952.1,"You have a special purpose as a nation and as a people."],[1955.22,"You're special to God in certain ways."],[1957.94,"But that means you have to follow through on that calling."],[1963.94,"And God's going to hold you accountable to that special calling."],[1968.18,"In a way that He isn't necessarily going to hold the other nations and other people from those nations accountable."],[1975.22,"And this is a broadly true principle, for all of us."],[1987.42,"We're the true church."],[1988.86,"We have the true faith."],[1990.06,"We're the real Christianity."],[1991.5,"Neener Niener evangelicals."],[1993.6,"We can get that way."],[1994.96,"Okay. But how many of the people doing that Niener Niener evangelicals that we're the true church and we're the true faith actually follow the fast and keep their prayer rule and attend every liturgy."],[2012.33,"That's being part of the true church, uh, like being an Israelite, and five bucks will get. you a cup of coffee at Starbucks"],[2025.14,"In fact, if anything, you're gonna be more accountable if you knew more about Christ and didn't follow him than someone who knew less, but was doing the best they could with what they knew."],[2039.22,"So this is a generally true principle."],[2041.78,"But this conditions, again, this is conditioning and nuancing in important ways what it means that Israel, later Judah, are God's chosen people."],[2053.48,"They're chosen for a purpose that has to be fulfilled and according to which they're going to be judged."],[2061.8,"Then the Lord will scatter you among all the nations, and you will be left few in number among the nations where the Lord will bring you."],[2068.24,"There you will serve different gods, the works of men's hands, wood and stone, which neither see, hear, eat, nor smell."],[2076.32,"But from there you will seek the Lord your God, and you will find him, when you seek him with all your heart, and with all your soul in your tribulation."],[2085.52,"And all these words will find you at the end of days, when you turn to the Lord your God and obey his voice."],[2091.84,"For the Lord your God is a merciful God, he will not forsake you, nor annihilate you, nor forget the covenant of your fathers which he swore to them."],[2101.2,"And so Moses, who actually is a prophet, just laid out the whole history of Israel to them."],[2109.12,"Not because I have a vision."],[2110.48,"He didn't even need that, because he knows them"],[2115.86,"He just spent 40 years with them."],[2118.26,"But more than even he knows them, he knows himself at this point."],[2122.82,"Doesn't this sound a lot like Moses' life?"],[2126.1,"Ran away from Egypt after he murdered somebody."],[2131.3,"Spent another 40 years."],[2133.76,"And then found God."],[2137.52,"And then came back."],[2139.44,"Also sounds a lot like the story of the prodigal son."],[2143.92,"Sounds a lot like the story of Adam."],[2147.01,"So this is the history, sort of fractally, of God and his people."],[2154.89,"I say fractally because you could go down to just about any person."],[2158.65,"Or you can go out to Israel, the church."],[2163.09,"That we start out, and this is this is a different, so our Protestant friends have."],[2170.13,"Notice this narrative's a little different."],[2172.19,"The Protestant narrative is sort of you start out uh condemned to hell, like when you're born."],[2180.77,"And then depending if you're a Calvinist, maybe God picked you, and so you end up becoming a Christian."],[2185.63,"Or, you know, otherwise, you know, you find God at some point in your life."],[2190.21,"And then you're good."],[2191.97,"That's it. But that's not that's not the narrative here."],[2194.93,"That's not the prodigal son."],[2196.13,"The Bible starts there in Eden"],[2196.97,"That's not the Bible."],[2203.77,"Prodigal son starts with them, him growing up in his father's house."],[2211.13,"This starts with God giving them the land and them going to dwell in it, and him having revealed himself to them and given them the Torah and given them the wisdom to follow him."],[2222.33,"But what happens?"],[2223.37,"They rebel, they fall away, they mess up, they lose that original, that's your original status."],[2231.66,"And then they go through very dark and hard times."],[2235.34,"And then there's repentance."],[2235.9,"'s repentance. There"],[2237.7,"You will find God when you turn and you seek him with your whole heart."],[2242.48,"There's return to God."],[2245.36,"There's a re-establishment."],[2246.8,"God doesn't strike them down in his wrath as soon as they leave."],[2253.52,"So this is the whole ark of the Bible."],[2255.28,"Starts at Eden, social paradise."],[2258.08,"Ends at the end of the book of Revelation."],[2260.0,"You want the ark of the whole Bible, there it is."],[2265.76,"Or Israel in the Old Testament."],[2269.52,"Exile and return."],[2271.52,"Kingdom, exile, return."],[2274.0,"Or many of us in our lives."],[2278.32,"And so Moses' prophet is not just predicting the future of what's going to happen to the nation of Israel."],[2283.84,"Moses is a prophet has been in heaven with God."],[2287.88,"Right on top of the mountain."],[2289.48,"And so he's seen these patterns."],[2294.3,"And understands them at this deep level."],[2296.7,"Because this story, as it applies to the nation of Israel, is something that no one he's talking to will live to see."],[2304.48,"The people here are going to live what?"],[2305.84,"Another 40 years?"],[2307.36,"50? They're still going to be in the land 50 years later."],[2311.62,"They're not none of this all isn't going to unfold."],[2314.18,"But in their in the lives of the people there, this narrative can very well unfold."],[2321.62,"For each of them."],[2324.42,"Verse 32, for ask now concerning former days."],[2328.58,"Before your day, in which God created man on the earth, and ask from one end of heaven to the other, whether any great thing like this has happened, or anything like it has been heard."],[2341.74,"Did any people ever hear the voice of the living God speaking from the midst of the fire, in the manner you heard and live?"],[2348.86,"Or did God ever try to go and take for himself a nation from the midst of another nation, in testing signs, wonders, and war, and by a mighty hand and outstretched arm, and by great visions according to all the Lord your God did for you in Egypt before your eyes."],[2364.22,"To you it was shown that you might know the Lord your God is God, so Yahweh your God is God."],[2370.62,"There is none other besides him."],[2373.42,"Now, besides is a bad translation."],[2376.18,"It's beside, alongside him."],[2380.35,"There is no one else like him."],[2382.27,"Out of heaven he let you hear his voice, that he might instruct you, and on earth he showed you his great fire, and you heard his words from the midst of the fire, because he loved your fathers, therefore he chose you their seed after them, and he brought you out of Egypt with his great strength, destroying from before your face nations greater and mightier than you, to bring you in to give you their land as an inheritance, as you have it today."],[2409.07,"So, again, we just had a big section where he was arguing you're not special."],[2413.33,"You get into the land and you disobey, you're gonna be wiped out."],[2416.05,"And now what do we go back to?"],[2418.89,"But look at how special you are."],[2420.41,"When has God ever done something like this before?"],[2423.71,"You're special, you're not special, you're special."],[2427.82,"Like this is this ongoing tension."],[2431.58,"But this is also, this is also why they can trust in God's mercy."],[2440.3,"Because what he's just told them is going to happen for the nation and for each of them is that there's going to be this falling away."],[2446.78,"It's going to be this falling away into sin, into idolatry, into all of these other things."],[2451.94,"Who's to say God would take them back?"],[2456.5,"I mean, Moses just said that."],[2457.94,"Moses said, when you turn back to God, God will take you back."],[2460.58,"You'll be forgiven"],[2462.68,"But why should they believe that?"],[2464.44,"That's not something any of the other gods, any of the other nations would do."],[2469.16,"Moses is telling them why they should believe that."],[2472.2,"Because look at what he already did for you."],[2476.52,"You think he's going to do all that and then just be like, oh, well, that didn't pan out."],[2483.85,"And this again, this is an argument St."],[2486.01,"Paul makes in Romans that he gets from here in Deuteronomy."],[2490.27,"Because he's talking to Christians about how do you know God's going to forgive you?"],[2494.67,"How do you know God's going to take you back?"],[2496.35,"How do you know God's going to receive you back when you've done the same dumb thing for the hundredth time?"],[2502.35,"And you wish you felt more bad about it than you do, if you're honest."],[2507.11,"What makes you think he's going to take you back?"],[2509.27,"What does St."],[2509.99,"Paul say? Look at what Christ already did for you."],[2514.87,"Look at what he already suffered for you."],[2517.99,"Look at what he already went."],[2519.35,"You think he's just going to be like, oh well, I guess that didn't pan out."],[2523.19,"Of course not."],[2525.11,"Of course not."],[2526.95,"That shows his love for you."],[2529.75,"The love he's talking about here."],[2532.47,"Because he loves you, he will take you back when you come back."],[2537.13,"Because he loves you, he's not going to smite you and wipe you out the first time you blow it."],[2542.69,"That's how you can know."],[2544.29,"Because you've already seen what he's done for you."],[2546.45,"Because you've seen that, you can know. for sure that when you repent, he will receive you back"],[2552.49,"Therefore, know today, and hear in mind, the Lord your God, this God, is in heaven above and on the earth beneath."],[2560.33,"There is no other beside him."],[2562.17,"You shall therefore guard his ordinances and his commandments."],[2565.53,"I command you today that it may be well with you and with your sons after you, and may prolong your days in the land the Lord your God is giving you to guard all the time."],[2574.65,"So that's the end of this first piece of discourse."],[2577.85,"And now we have this little linking piece, and then him talking is going to pick up."],[2582.33,"But so to read this little linking piece."],[2584.89,"Then Moses set apart three cities beyond the Jordan toward the rising of the sun."],[2588.97,"So the manslayer who kills his neighbor without foreknowledge, without hating him previously, might flee into one of these cities and live there."],[2596.85,"Bezer in the desert on the plateau for Reuben, Remot and Gilead for Gad, and Golan and Bashan for Manasseh."],[2604.05,"As we said, Bashan is now the Golan Heights."],[2606.21,"So there you go."],[2607.09,"Notice something here, though, real quickly."],[2609.49,"Remember when we first read about the cities of refuge, what it said?"],[2612.53,"That the cities of refuge were there at the end of Numbers?"],[2614.77,"Cities of refuge were there for someone who killed unintentionally."],[2620.23,"And we talked about this whole weird meme now in Old Testament studies, and a lot of people online and stuff saying that like there was no forgiveness for intentional sins."],[2632.41,"In the Old Testament."],[2633.69,"And I've kind of joked about like, oh, so you had to pay back five times if you stole unintentionally."],[2636.25,"Like now that doesn't really make sense"],[2642.67,"Like, oops, I committed adultery."],[2644.69,"Like, so, that doesn't make a lot of sense."],[2647.18,"Well, notice how, so this is the same, same cities for the same purpose."],[2651.8,"But how is unintentional defined here?"],[2655.96,"Without foreknowledge, without hating him previously."],[2662.52,"That's how unintentional is defined."],[2665.88,"Okay. So that's why when we were talking about that, I connected the idea of intentional and unintentional to repentance."],[2675.5,"And to deliberateness."],[2677.52,"Deliberation. So this is like our distinction between first degree murder and second degree murder."],[2683.19,"First degree murder is premeditated."],[2684.87,"It's the same kind of idea."],[2687.11,"So under this, somebody getting angry in the moment and killing someone would be considered unintentional."],[2697.03,"So that's a very different view of unintentional than the one that those folks want to give."],[2703.56,"Now this is the law Moses set before the sons of Israel."],[2706.76,"These are the testimonies, the ordinances."],[2708.76,"This is introducing the part we're about to start."],[2710.94,"So this is talking about this change in topic."],[2713.66,"These are the testimonies and ordinances and the judgments Moses spoke to the sons of Israel in the desert after they came out of Egypt, beyond the Jordan, in the valley near Beth Peor, in the land of Sihon, king of the Amorites, who dwell in Heshbon, whom Moses and the children of Israel defeated after they came out of Egypt."],[2733.7,"So they inherited his land in the land of Og, king of Bashan, two kings of the Amorites, beyond the Jordan toward the rising of the sun."],[2741.38,"So they keep talking about Sihon and Og getting cacked."],[2744.18,"That's the whole thing."],[2746.18,"From Aror, which is on the bank of the Arnon River, even to Mount Sion, that is Hermon, and all the Arabah beyond the Jordan, toward the rising of the sun, below Asadot, hewn in the rock."],[2761.54,"So, yes, that's introducing what we're about to get into."],[2764.66,"Not right now, but next time."],[2767.26,"Uh in Deuteronomy chapter five, we're gonna get a reiteration of some of an expansion and application of some of the commandments that we've seen previously."],[2777.42,"So, in closing, and this is mostly for the recording, but this is an important benchmark."],[2782.78,"Cause something like 13 and a half years ago, maybe 14 years ago, I started recording this Bible study."],[2793.42,"Some of you may know, with Deuteronomy chapter five."],[2797.02,"So that means that as of this recording, there are now recordings of me talking about the entire Bible."],[2803.9,"Uh a good chunk of them are potato quality, and so we will continue to replace those."],[2809.74,"So we're gonna keep going and recording and replace all those old ones."],[2813.38,"But it's still kind of a benchmark that now, if so inclined, if you have a long enough commute."],[2820.66,"If you're flying to Australia, you can listen to me talk about every verse in the entire Bible now and cure your insomnia possibly permanently."],[2830.9,"But that's it for now, so thank you, everybody."],[2835.7,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2842.98,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2848.34,"That's whole counsel at ancientfaith.com"]],"o":[{"t":22.64,"lv":2,"h":"4:14-18 - You saw no form","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:14</b> Lord commanded Moses to <b>teach ordinances and judgments</b> to observe in the land</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:15-18</b> \"guard your souls, for you <b>saw no form</b> when the Lord spoke at <b>Horeb</b> from the fire\"</li><li class=\"d1\">don't \"act lawlessly\" and make a <b>carved form</b> of any image</li><li class=\"d1\">likeness of <b>male or female</b>, <b>cattle</b>, <b>winged bird</b>, <b>creeping thing</b>, <b>fish</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"When you were there you <b>didn't see anybody</b>\" - true of the people</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Moses did see somebody</b> - but made <b>no images</b> of him</li><li class=\"d1\">\"otherwise we'd have <b>way older icons of Christ</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"Therefore\"</b> - the reason they're not to make images <b>of God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"you didn't see God's form, therefore you can't draw your <b>pet goldfish</b>\" - no logic</li><li class=\"d1\">not a ban on drawing your dad: about <b>depicting God</b></li></ul>"},{"t":141.42,"lv":3,"h":"Golden calf and idolatry","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Listed forms = what the <b>surrounding nations</b> gave to the <b>divine / their gods</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Rules out what they did with the <b>golden calf</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Aaron</b> didn't say \"let's worship <b>Baal</b> now\"</li><li class=\"d1\">made a calf, built an altar: <b>\"This is Yahweh who brought you out of Egypt\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">So: no <b>depictions of God</b>, because they <b>had not seen him</b></li></ul>"},{"t":178.66,"lv":3,"h":"Imagination: making God in our image","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Core = <b>imagination</b> - humans making God <b>in their image</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Idols used to <b>manipulate and control the gods</b></li><li class=\"d1\">literal ritual sense: \"we bring you offerings, you give us this\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>subtle</b> sense: I come up with an idea of God <b>congenial to me</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Still pertinent: \"<b>their own personal Jesus</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">hears their prayers, <b>loves them just the way they are</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>never asks them to do anything</b> they don't want, always on their side</li><li class=\"d1\">sure to take them to heaven; loves <b>pistachio ice cream</b>, hates <b>broccoli</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Unsubtle version: <b>three quests for the historical Jesus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">very smart scholars produced a \"real Jesus\" who <b>looked a lot like them</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>charismatic</b> scholar → charismatic Jesus; <b>ascetical</b> Roman Catholic → strict Jesus</li><li class=\"d0\">That God/Jesus <b>doesn't exist</b> → <b>can't save you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">can't follow him: \"he's not leading you anywhere, you've made him <b>exactly where you are</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">no growing, changing, <b>repenting</b> → leads you <b>deeper into sin</b>, toward <b>destruction</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moses: \"don't go there\"</li></ul>"},{"t":362.74,"lv":2,"h":"Icons and the incarnation","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Passage raised in the <b>8th century</b> iconography arguments</li><li class=\"d0\">Fathers: this is why <b>icons of Christ</b> are tied to the <b>incarnation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"at that time they saw <b>no form</b>. <b>We saw Jesus</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just rhetoric - over and over in the <b>New Testament</b></li><li class=\"d1\">end of <b>John's prologue</b>: \"No one has seen God at any time. The unique Son… <b>has made him known</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Peter</b>: \"what we have <b>seen</b>, what we have <b>touched</b> with our hands\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Theological point: <b>this has changed</b> - now the people of God have <b>all seen God</b></li></ul>"},{"t":425.88,"lv":3,"h":"Only Christ as Christ","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Rule: depict <b>Christ only as Christ</b>, as he appeared</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not as a sheep</b> - \"very common in the West\"; \"seems crazy\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Orthodox iconography takes it to <b>weirdness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">icon of the <b>paten (<i>diskos</i>)</b> with the <b>Lamb</b> in the Eucharist</li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't show a piece of bread - shows a <b>tiny Jesus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">after <b>consecration</b> the Lamb <b>is Christ</b> → depicted as Christ</li><li class=\"d1\">\"that's how <b>strict</b> this rule is\"</li></ul>"},{"t":501.5,"lv":3,"h":"Saints and figures are not idolatry","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Text says <b>nothing</b> about icons of <b>saints and other Bible figures</b> - \"not idolatry\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Someone tried a case <b>against iconography from the fathers</b></li><li class=\"d1\">every quote = fathers criticizing <b>pagans</b> depicting the divine as <b>humans and animals</b> - exactly <b>Moses' critique</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"that's <b>not what iconography is</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Icon of <b>St. Paul</b> = <b>portrait of a human</b>, looks as Paul did</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Christ</b> is divine - but not imagining or depicting as an animal: <b>as he appeared</b></li><li class=\"d0\">In one sense <b>Christ changes this</b>: now a way of depicting God</li><li class=\"d0\">In another sense <b>nothing changed</b>: <b>exclusion of imagination and idolatry</b> fully accepted</li></ul>"},{"t":595.54,"lv":2,"h":"Q: How did Roman Catholic depictions stray?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: how did <b>Roman Catholic</b> depictions of Jesus come <b>stray from the truth</b>?</li><li class=\"d0\">A: <b>Pope</b> accepted, rejected, accepted again the <b>Seventh Ecumenical Council</b> (<b>787</b>, iconography)</li><li class=\"d1\">reason: <b>Charlemagne</b></li><li class=\"d1\">didn't dislike icons - disliked the <b>positive theology of icons</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Debate included whether the <b>Eucharist is an icon</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>iconoclasts</b>: only real icon of Christ = Eucharist, since an icon must be <i>homoousios</i> with its prototype - \"something they made up\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Nicaea II</b> affirmed the Eucharist is <b>not an icon</b> - \"not something you look at\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>West</b> already disagreed - wanted the Eucharist as an icon</li><li class=\"d1\">also didn't accept the <b>positive view</b> of the 7th and 8th councils (8th, 9th c., also dealt with this)</li><li class=\"d1\">for them iconography = <b>art for educational purposes</b></li><li class=\"d1\">so no problem with <b>imagination</b> - which he'd argue <b>comes from Deuteronomy</b></li></ul>"},{"t":723.5,"lv":3,"h":"<i>Libri Carolini</i> and Eucharistic adoration","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Libri Carolini</b>, Western <b>Frankish councils</b>: <b>Charlemagne's court theologians</b> → a different theology of iconography</li><li class=\"d0\">Goes <b>two directions</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Eucharistic adoration</b> begins: Eucharist <b>elevated</b>, put in a <b>monstrance</b>, <b>worshiped</b> - \"never a thing in the East\"</li><li class=\"d1\">East: \"the Eucharist is <b>for eating, not looking at</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">other direction: <b>art just becomes art</b>, <b>imagination allowed</b></li></ul>"},{"t":770.38,"lv":3,"h":"Western art, halos, and statues","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Early Western art <b>looks like iconography</b> in broad strokes</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Theotokos and infant Christ</b> in the same pose</li><li class=\"d1\">then <b>imagination</b> creeps in: colors, <b>more realistic faces</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Renaissance</b>: <b>live models</b> for saints, <b>perspective</b></li><li class=\"d0\">East: Christian art is fine, but <b>not iconography</b></li><li class=\"d1\">iconography has <b>strict rules</b> of color, presentation</li><li class=\"d1\">you could have <b>heretical iconography</b> (bad theology)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Halo / nimbus</b>: <b>Moses</b> - glory of God reflected in the face</li><li class=\"d1\">West <b>forgot what it was about</b> → floating circle → cartoon <b>golden ring</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Michelangelo's Moses with horns</b> - mistranslation</li><li class=\"d0\">Pre-1000: <b>relics</b> bigger in the West, <b>icons</b> bigger in the East</li><li class=\"d1\">West got a <b>looser view</b>; 7th Council accepted \"through a lens\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Statues</b>: no Orthodox rule against them - but iconography must follow <b>ancient models</b>, and none for statuary</li><li class=\"d1\">an imaginative statue can't qualify as an icon</li><li class=\"d1\">dig up a <b>2nd-century statue</b> → could reproduce it; we have <b>bas relief</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1014.24,"lv":2,"h":"Q: Is the Eucharist an icon in Rome?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: does the Roman church <b>still</b> hold the Eucharist is an icon? How with <b>real presence</b>?</li><li class=\"d0\">A: in <b>Eucharistic adoration</b> it's treated as one</li><li class=\"d1\">they <b>worship</b> rather than venerate - \"it's Christ himself\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Other Eucharistic developments: <b>host alone</b> = <b>body, blood, soul, and divinity</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"gobbledygook to us\" - \"he said, <b>This is my body</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">their logic: can't separate body and blood, or from <b>divinity</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"we're <b>not Nestorians</b>\" - we say: it <b>really is</b> his body</li></ul>"},{"t":1092.24,"lv":2,"h":"4:19-20 - Sun, moon, and stars","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:19</b> \"Idolatry, right out.\" Also don't, lifting eyes to <b>sun, moon, stars</b>, go astray and <b>worship and serve</b> them</li><li class=\"d1\">\"which the Lord assigned to <b>all the nations</b> under heaven\"</li><li class=\"d0\">He's not happy with the <b>footnote</b> in the translation</li><li class=\"d0\">Problem: we look at them <b>very differently</b> than ancient people</li><li class=\"d1\">moon = <b>big rock</b> orbiting; landed on it - <b>\"offended flat earthers\"</b>; Chinese <b>rovers</b></li><li class=\"d1\">sun = massive <b>incandescent gas / plasma</b>; <b>hydrogen fusion</b> into helium</li><li class=\"d0\">Not how ancients saw them; not what Moses means</li><li class=\"d1\">modern readers: \"don't worship rocks and sticks - and those are <b>rocks and sticks in space</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>nobody</b> who wrote or heard this thought so</li><li class=\"d1\">they're <b>angels</b> (or <b>gods</b> to a pagan) <b>moving around in the heavens</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Spirits</b> associated with these things</li></ul>"},{"t":1249.08,"lv":2,"h":"Angels and the lights of Genesis 1","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Genesis 1</b>, <b>fourth day</b>: sun, moon, stars created to <b>govern day and night</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just \"the sun looks in charge during the day\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Fathers: one of the days the <b>angels were created</b></li><li class=\"d1\">usually <b>first day</b> or <b>fourth day</b> - connected: light created, then the <b>lights</b> in particular</li><li class=\"d0\">Angels <b>govern and administer</b> the world</li></ul>"},{"t":1320.3,"lv":3,"h":"Why God has angels: love, not need","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Why does God <b>need</b> that?\" - <b>he doesn't</b></li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't need <b>me or you</b> - created us <b>out of love</b></li><li class=\"d1\">can <b>heal without my praying</b>: \"if we don't get enough <b>likes on this Facebook post</b> the kid's gonna die of cancer\" - not how it works</li><li class=\"d1\">gives the <b>privilege</b> of working through prayers - \"I get to be a part of God's healing\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Angels</b> for the same reason - <b>no necessity</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God shows up <b>in person</b> all the time, talks to Moses</li><li class=\"d0\">Out of love creates beings other than himself, <b>shares his life</b></li><li class=\"d1\">takes the form of <b>governance and administration</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Promise to humans</b> = source of <i>theosis</i></li><li class=\"d1\">glorified after death, given a place in it</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Revelation</b>: \"come alive and <b>rule and reign with Christ</b>\" - <b>Christ doesn't need co-rulers</b>, but shares it</li></ul>"},{"t":1453.63,"lv":3,"h":"Nations worship the angels","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Philo</b>: God assigned <b>angelic beings</b> to help govern <b>all the nations</b></li><li class=\"d1\">more about this at the <b>end of Deuteronomy</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Nations start worshiping them <b>as gods</b> in their majesty</li><li class=\"d1\">start thinking they <b>control human destiny</b> - <b>astrology</b>, \"way bigger in the ancient world\"</li><li class=\"d1\">they control things, <b>you need to worship them</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Basic mistake</b>: giving <b>God's glory</b> to a <b>created being</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moses: <b>they do that - you don't</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not just \"don't worship sun gods, moon gods\" - <b>all pagans</b> worship <b>spirits God created</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"creatures just like you and me\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1557.16,"lv":2,"h":"Good angels refuse worship","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Good angel</b> appears in the Bible → someone <b>falls down to worship</b> almost immediately</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>Get up off the ground.</b> I'm a created being just like you… a <b>servant of God</b> just like you. <b>Worship him</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">True through the Bible; seen in <b>Revelation</b> not long ago</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Stars</b> almost always = <b>angels</b> - how ancients understood it</li><li class=\"d0\">Two pieces: <b>don't worship God using idols</b>, then <b>don't worship the nations' gods</b></li><li class=\"d1\">reason: <b>not because they're imaginary or don't exist</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they're <b>spirits created by God</b> - worship the <b>true God</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1638.07,"lv":2,"h":"4:20-24 - Iron furnace, consuming fire","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:20</b> Lord took you out of the <b>iron furnace</b> from Egypt to be his <b>people, an inheritance</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:21-22</b> Lord <b>angry with Moses</b> because of what <b>you</b> said: swore he would <b>not cross the Jordan</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I am going to <b>die in this land</b>\" - <b>you</b> will cross and inherit the good land</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:23-24</b> \"take heed… lest you <b>forget the covenant</b>\" and make a carved form</li><li class=\"d1\">\"the Lord your God is a <b>consuming fire</b>, a <b>jealous God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Others do that - <b>you're not like the other nations</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God didn't <b>rescue other nations</b> out of Egypt</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>formed Israel as a nation out of nothing</b> - not individuals, the <b>nation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">didn't choose one nation: <b>made a new one</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God <b>revealed himself directly</b> → worship <b>just him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">won't tolerate also worshiping those <b>other spirits</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1730.4,"lv":2,"h":"4:25-28 - Heaven and earth as witnesses","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:25-26</b> sons and grandsons, long in the land, act lawlessly, carved form, <b>provoke him to anger</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I call <b>heaven and earth</b> to witness… <b>utterly destroyed</b> from the land\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>annihilated</b>; won't live long on it</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Moses is being <b>really mean</b>\" - \"we all need to be nice\" - but he's <b>not cursing</b> them</li><li class=\"d1\">saying a <b>curse will come</b> if they do this</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Two witnesses</b>: how anything is established in court in the Torah</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>heavens above</b>, <b>earth</b> you live on - they'll <b>know what you do</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Why so drastic? About to enter the land and <b>wipe out certain groups</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God: \"if you <b>become like them</b>, you'll get wiped out too\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1823.31,"lv":3,"h":"Special, but not special","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">First four chapters (esp. <b>ch. 2</b>): Moses keeps saying <b>\"you're special, but you're not special\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God loving you and bringing you out of Egypt ≠ he'll <b>let it slide more</b> than other nations</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>quite the opposite</b></li><li class=\"d1\">only nation given the <b>Torah</b>, with <b>God dwelling in your midst</b>, sent <b>prophets</b></li><li class=\"d1\">→ <b>more accountable and responsible</b>: \"expect <b>less patience</b>, more accountability\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Same argument as <b>Paul in Romans 1 and 2</b>, getting it from Deuteronomy</li><li class=\"d1\">\"it's not the <b>hearers</b> of the law, it's the <b>doers</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">hearing commandments every <b>Sabbath</b> means nothing if you didn't do them</li><li class=\"d1\">\"in the same boat as the <b>Roman</b> who didn't do it\" - he may be due <b>more mercy</b>, <b>never heard it</b>, an excuse</li><li class=\"d0\">Ongoing theme through Deuteronomy: special <b>calling</b>, held <b>accountable</b> to it</li></ul>"},{"t":1975.22,"lv":2,"h":"A principle for us too","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Broadly true for all of us</li><li class=\"d0\">\"We're the <b>true church</b>, we have the true faith\" - <b>\"Neener neener evangelicals\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">how many actually <b>follow the fast, keep the prayer rule, attend every liturgy</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">being part of the true church like being an Israelite - \"<b>five bucks will get you a cup of coffee at Starbucks</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">More accountable if you <b>knew more about Christ</b> and didn't follow him than someone who knew less, <b>doing their best</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Conditions and nuances</b> what it means that Israel, later Judah, are <b>God's chosen people</b></li><li class=\"d1\">chosen for a <b>purpose</b> that must be fulfilled - <b>judged</b> according to it</li></ul>"},{"t":2061.8,"lv":2,"h":"4:27-31 - Scattered, then seek and find","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:27-28</b> Lord will <b>scatter you among all the nations</b>, <b>few in number</b></li><li class=\"d1\">there you <b>serve different gods</b>, wood and stone - <b>neither see, hear, eat, nor smell</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:29-30</b> \"from there you will <b>seek the Lord</b> and <b>find him</b>\" with <b>all your heart and soul</b>, in <b>tribulation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">words find you <b>at the end of days</b> when you turn and obey</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:31</b> \"a <b>merciful God</b>, he will not forsake you, nor annihilate you, nor forget the <b>covenant of your fathers</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses, a prophet, lays out <b>the whole history of Israel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not a vision - he <b>knows them</b>, spent <b>40 years</b> with them</li><li class=\"d1\">more: he <b>knows himself</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2122.82,"lv":3,"h":"The fractal story of God and his people","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Doesn't this sound a lot like <b>Moses' life</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">ran from Egypt after <b>murdering</b> somebody, <b>another 40 years</b>, found God, <b>came back</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Also the <b>prodigal son</b>; also <b>Adam</b></li><li class=\"d0\">History <b>fractally</b> of God and his people - down to <b>one person</b>, out to <b>Israel, the church</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Protestant narrative</b> differs: born <b>condemned to hell</b>; if <b>Calvinist</b>, God picked you; find God, \"then you're good\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not the Bible's narrative</b>, not the prodigal son</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Prodigal son</b> starts growing up in his <b>father's house</b></li><li class=\"d1\">here: God gives the land, reveals himself, gives the Torah and <b>wisdom</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they <b>rebel, fall away</b>, lose original status → <b>dark, hard times</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>repentance</b> - \"you will find God when you seek him with your whole heart\" - <b>return, re-establishment</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God doesn't <b>strike them down</b> as soon as they leave</li><li class=\"d0\">The <b>arc of the whole Bible</b>: <b>Eden, paradise</b> → end of <b>Revelation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">also <b>Israel</b>: kingdom, exile, return; also <b>many of us</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2278.32,"lv":2,"h":"Moses as prophet","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Not just predicting Israel's future: Moses <b>has been in heaven with God</b>, on top of the mountain</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>seen these patterns</b>, understands them <b>deeply</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Story as applied to the nation <b>no one there will live to see</b> - they'll live another <b>40-50 years</b> in the land</li><li class=\"d0\">But in the <b>lives of the people there</b> this narrative <b>can unfold</b> - for <b>each of them</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2324.42,"lv":2,"h":"4:32-38 - Has any God done this?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:32-33</b> \"ask concerning <b>former days</b>\" - since God <b>created man</b>, from one end of heaven to the other</li><li class=\"d1\">did any people <b>hear the voice of the living God</b> from the fire <b>and live</b>?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:34</b> did God ever <b>take a nation from the midst of another nation</b> - <b>testing signs, wonders, war, mighty hand and outstretched arm</b>, great visions - in Egypt before your eyes</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:35</b> \"that you might know <b>Yahweh your God is God</b>. There is none other <b>besides him</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>\"besides\" is a bad translation</b> - it's <b>beside, alongside him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>no one else like him</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:36-38</b> from heaven let you hear his voice, on earth showed his <b>great fire</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"because he <b>loved your fathers</b>\" → chose their seed, brought you out with <b>great strength</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>destroying nations greater and mightier</b>, giving you their land</li></ul>"},{"t":2409.07,"lv":3,"h":"Why Israel can trust God's mercy","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Just had \"you're <b>not special</b>… wiped out\" - now <b>\"look how special you are\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"special, not special, special\" - <b>ongoing tension</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Also why they can <b>trust God's mercy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">he just said there will be a <b>falling away</b> into sin and idolatry</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>who's to say God would take them back?</b>\" - no other nation's god would</li><li class=\"d1\">Moses tells them why: <b>look at what he already did for you</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same argument <b>Paul</b> makes in <b>Romans</b>, from Deuteronomy</li><li class=\"d1\">Christians: how do you know God will forgive you the <b>hundredth time</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">\"you wish you felt <b>more bad</b> about it than you do, if you're honest\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul: <b>look at what Christ already did and suffered for you</b> - \"you think he's going to say, <b>oh well, that didn't pan out</b>?\" - \"of course not\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Because he loves you</b>, he'll take you back; won't <b>smite</b> you the first time you blow it</li><li class=\"d1\">\"because you've seen what he's done, you can know <b>for sure</b> he'll receive you back\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2552.49,"lv":2,"h":"4:39-40 - Know today","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:39</b> \"<b>Know today</b>, and keep in mind: the Lord your God… is in <b>heaven above and on the earth beneath</b>. <b>No other beside him</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>4:40</b> \"<b>guard his ordinances and commandments</b>\" that it may be <b>well with you and your sons</b> and you <b>prolong your days</b> in the land</li><li class=\"d0\">End of this <b>first piece of discourse</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Now a <b>linking piece</b>, then Moses picks up again</li></ul>"},{"t":2584.89,"lv":2,"h":"4:41-43 - Cities of refuge","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Moses <b>set apart three cities</b> beyond the Jordan, <b>toward the rising of the sun</b></li><li class=\"d1\">for the <b>manslayer</b> who kills <b>without foreknowledge</b>, <b>without hating him previously</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Bezer</b> (Reuben, on the plateau), <b>Ramoth in Gilead</b> (Gad), <b>Golan in Bashan</b> (Manasseh)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Bashan</b> = now the <b>Golan Heights</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2607.09,"lv":3,"h":"\"Unintentional\" defined","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Cities of refuge first appear at <b>end of Numbers</b>, for <b>unintentional</b> killing</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Meme</b> in OT studies / online: <b>no forgiveness for intentional sins</b></li><li class=\"d1\">joke: \"you had to pay back <b>five times</b> if you stole unintentionally\" - doesn't make sense</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>oops, I committed adultery</b>\" - doesn't make sense either</li><li class=\"d0\">Same cities, same purpose - how is it <b>defined</b> here?</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>\"without foreknowledge, without hating him previously\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">So <b>intentional / unintentional</b> connects to <b>repentance</b> and <b>deliberation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">like <b>first-degree murder</b> = <b>premeditated</b></li><li class=\"d1\">killing someone <b>angry in the moment</b> = <b>unintentional</b></li><li class=\"d1\">very different from the view those folks want to give</li></ul>"},{"t":2703.56,"lv":2,"h":"4:44-49 - Introduction to the law","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"This is the <b>law</b> Moses set before the sons of Israel\" - <b>testimonies, ordinances, judgments</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>introduces the part we're about to start</b> - change in topic</li><li class=\"d0\">Spoken <b>in the desert</b> after coming out of Egypt, <b>beyond the Jordan</b>, in the valley near <b>Beth-peor</b></li><li class=\"d1\">in the land of <b>Sihon, king of the Amorites</b>, in <b>Heshbon</b></li><li class=\"d1\">also land of <b>Og, king of Bashan</b> - \"two kings of the Amorites\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"They keep talking about Sihon and Og <b>getting cacked</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Land: from <b>Aroer</b> on the <b>Arnon</b> to <b>Mount Sion (Hermon)</b>, all the <b>Arabah</b> beyond the Jordan, below <b>Asdot</b>, hewn in the rock</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Deuteronomy 5</b>: reiteration, <b>expansion and application</b> of commandments seen before</li></ul>"},{"t":2777.42,"lv":2,"h":"Benchmark: the whole Bible recorded","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Mostly for the recording - an important <b>benchmark</b></li><li class=\"d0\">~<b>13.5 or 14 years ago</b> he started recording this Bible study</li><li class=\"d1\">began with <b>Deuteronomy chapter 5</b></li><li class=\"d0\">As of this recording: <b>recordings of him talking about the entire Bible</b></li><li class=\"d1\">a good chunk \"<b>potato quality</b>\" - will keep going and <b>replace</b> them</li><li class=\"d0\">\"If you're flying to <b>Australia</b>, you can listen to me talk about <b>every verse</b> in the Bible and <b>cure your insomnia</b> possibly permanently\"</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next time: <b>Deuteronomy 5</b> - reiteration and application of the commandments"});
